Populate the shade page from the style constants

The custom shades page shows the values that the style uses while a
group is off. Three of the shown values were wrong.

The two etch alpha boxes crossed their constants. The style reads the
light alpha where ETCH_BOTTOM_ALPHA stands. It reads the dark alpha
where ETCH_TOP_ALPHA stands. The page filled the two boxes the other way
round, so a tick of the group box moved both etch alphas.

A change of the shading routine left the six shade boxes on the row of
the previous routine, because only the load filled them. A later tick of
the group box then wrote that stale row.

The shade values also ignored the darker borders adjustment, which takes
0.1 off the border shade. With darker borders on, a tick of the group
box lightened the border of every widget.

populateInternShades() now fills the boxes through qtcShadeGetIntern(),
which is the function that the style itself calls. The routine combo and
the darker borders box refill the boxes while the group is off.

The change sits on the branch work/dialog-state of the local tree, as commit 6 of 12.
A new merge request on system/qtcurve takes that branch.

Drop this patch when upstream merges the change.

